  "local_adaptations": {
    "reason": "Owner explicitly requested local hindsight-embed daemon with Codex-backed native memory instead of Docker on 2026-11-15. Reviewed-record bank remains separate and chunk-only. Review-runner children disable native memory hooks/MCP to preserve independent read-only review isolation. The standalone plan-review recipe and native architecture role also require an isolated parent/process. Owner switched the Codex model from gpt-6.1-sol to gpt-6.2-sol on 2026-11-18 (live call confirmed access); the routing policy, runner, validator, doctor text, Codex roles, plan-review recipe and model references in reference/skills docs carry that local model pin. Efforts and gates unchanged. Fresh reviews run in a disposable copy-on-write clone of the checkout with a private temp folder (policy/review-sandbox.json, read from the task's base commit), so they can run every project check (read-only real checkout in workspace-write mode); the user Codex config (and its MCP servers) is not loaded; the turn's processes are killed and the clone deleted afterwards; repair turns are pinned to the real checkout with -C. Network is on (accepted risk; owner decision 2026-11-18). Review turns use danger-full-access so browser checks can run (owner decision 2026-11-18; macOS's Codex sandbox refuses browsers); the runner rejects a review that changes source files, HEAD, the index, git config, hooks and info (with modes), the policy's protected refs (integration branches, tags, replace refs), shallow, object alternates or linked-worktree pointers (also after a timeout or failed cleanup); other branches and their upstream tracking settings, remote-tracking refs, stash, other worktrees added or deleted, ignored files, the run folder, git objects, hooksPath targets, included/global/submodule git config, paths outside the checkout and escaped processes are not detected. Kit docs that call reviews read-only mean review-only in full-access mode. Owner requested Sol cache/compaction/Hindsight review hygiene on 2026-11-24: set model_auto_compact_token_limit=390000 for gpt-6.2-sol (475k window) in .codex/config.toml and kit_codex.py, added HINDSIGHT_DISABLE_HOOKS=1 in kit_codex.py, added .agents/agent-kit/runtime/kit_sol_review.py (plus unit tests) for cache-safe read-only tiered Sol reviews (pinning effort/sandbox/hooks=false/agents=false/390k compact and dynamically disabling unused MCPs/plugins per scope), and updated AGENTS.md Rule 3 to require deterministic checks before review and kit_sol_review.py for tiered reviews. Added .agents/agent-kit/runtime/kit_efficiency_watchdog.py (zero-LLM deterministic efficiency watchdog for Codex/Sol cache drift, Hindsight leaks, premature compaction, wait storms, timeouts, pass caps, and oversized slices), wired inline into kit_sol_review.py and documented in AGENTS.md Rule 3. Reconciled manifest checksums on 2026-11-25 after reviewed .agents/ consolidation (3c6b0187), kit_context.py codex_config_path fix (19facdf3), and AGENTS.md cap tightening (e39c6bc4).",
